---
import { PRODUCT_NAME } from '../config';
import LegalPage from '../components/legal/LegalPage.astro';
import {
  CONFIRM, CONTACT_EMAIL, GOVERNING_LAW, LICENSOR, LICENSOR_COUNTRY, MACS_PER_LICENCE, OFFLINE_GRACE_DAYS, REFUND_DAYS, TRIAL_DAYS, VENUE,
} from '../components/legal/legal';

const toc = [
  { id: 'agreement', label: 'The agreement' },
  { id: 'grant', label: 'Licence grant' },
  { id: 'trial', label: 'Trial' },
  { id: 'updates', label: 'Lifetime updates' },
  { id: 'activation', label: 'Activation' },
  { id: 'restrictions', label: 'Restrictions' },
  { id: 'ownership', label: 'Ownership' },
  { id: 'open-source', label: 'Open-source components' },
  { id: 'termination', label: 'Termination' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: 'No warranty' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'general', label: 'General' },
];
---
<LegalPage
  title={`EULA · ${PRODUCT_NAME}`}
  heading="End User Licence Agreement"
  description={`The licence you accept when you install ${PRODUCT_NAME}: one payment, lifetime updates, up to ${MACS_PER_LICENCE} Macs per licence.`}
  ogTheme="light"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="agreement">1. The agreement</h2>
  <p>
    This End User Licence Agreement ("EULA") is between you and {LICENSOR}, an individual based in {LICENSOR_COUNTRY} ("Licensor", "we"), for the {PRODUCT_NAME} software for macOS, including updates and documentation (the "Software"). By installing or using the Software you agree to this
    EULA. If you don't agree, don't install or use it. Purchases are also covered by our <a href="/terms">terms of sale</a>.
  </p>
  <p>The Software is licensed, not sold. All rights reserved.</p>

  <h2 id="grant">2. Licence grant</h2>
  <p>When you buy a licence, we grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, perpetual licence to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>install and use the Software on up to <strong>{MACS_PER_LICENCE} Macs</strong> at the same time that you own or control;</li>
    <li>use it for any lawful purpose, personal or commercial, including on your employer's or clients' repositories.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A licence is for one person. A company buying for several people needs one licence per person who uses the Software.
  </p>

  <h2 id="trial">3. Trial</h2>
  <p>
    Before you buy, you may use the full Software for {TRIAL_DAYS} days to evaluate it. When the trial ends, the Software stays usable in
    read-only mode until you enter a licence key. Your repositories are never locked, hidden or deleted.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updates">4. Lifetime updates</h2>
  <p>
    Your licence covers every future version of the Software we publish, at no extra cost and without renewal. We aren't obliged to release
    updates, keep a particular feature or support every macOS version, but anything we release as {PRODUCT_NAME} is included.
  </p>

  <h2 id="activation">5. Activation and licence checks</h2>
  <p>
    The Software activates your key with Polar, our merchant of record, and checks it about once per session while you're online. It keeps
    working offline for up to {OFFLINE_GRACE_DAYS} days after the last successful check. The check sends only what the <a href="/privacy#app">privacy policy</a> lists. You can move a licence to another Mac by removing an old one in the Polar customer portal.
  </p>

  <h2 id="restrictions">6. Restrictions</h2>
  <p>Except as this EULA or applicable law expressly allows, you may not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>copy, distribute, sell, rent, lend, sublicense or otherwise make the Software or your licence key available to others;</li>
    <li>share or publish your licence key, or use it on more than {MACS_PER_LICENCE} Macs at once;</li>
    <li>remove, disable or bypass the trial, activation or licence checks;</li>
    <li>modify, translate or create derivative works of the Software, or decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer it, except to the extent the law permits despite this restriction;</li>
    <li>remove or alter any proprietary notices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ownership">7. Ownership</h2>
  <p>
    The Software, its source code, design and the {PRODUCT_NAME} name and logo belong to the Licensor and are protected by copyright and other laws.
    This EULA gives you no rights in them beyond the licence in section 2. Your repositories and everything in them remain entirely yours.
  </p>

  <h2 id="open-source">8. Open-source components</h2>
  <p>
    The Software includes open-source components, such as Electron and Chromium, and bundled fonts, each under its own licence. Those licences
    govern those components, and nothing in this EULA limits your rights under them. Their notices ship with the app and are listed separately
    from this EULA. <span class="legal-placeholder">{CONFIRM}</span>
  </p>
  <p>
    The Software runs the <code>git</code> program already installed on your Mac. Git is not part of the Software and is not distributed with it.
    Git™ is a trademark of Software Freedom Conservancy; {PRODUCT_NAME} is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Git project.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination">9. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    This licence lasts until it ends. It ends automatically if you materially breach this EULA, or if your purchase is refunded or charged back.
    When it ends, stop using the Software in licensed mode. Sections 7 to 12 survive termination. You can end it at any time by deleting the Software.
  </p>

  <h2 id="warranty">10. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The Software rewrites Git history and changes files. It records every ref change so you can undo it, but you are responsible for keeping
    backups of your work. Beyond our <a href="/refunds">{REFUND_DAYS}-day refund</a> and any rights you have by law that can't be excluded,
    the Software is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability,
    fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, or that it will be error-free or uninterrupted.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">11. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, the Licensor isn't liable for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for loss of
    data, profits, revenue or business, arising from your use of the Software, even if advised of the possibility. The Licensor's total liability
    under this EULA is limited to the amount you paid for your licence. Nothing in this EULA limits liability that can't be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="general">12. General</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Governing law:</strong> {GOVERNING_LAW}. <span class="legal-placeholder">{CONFIRM}</span></li>
    <li><strong>Venue:</strong> {VENUE}, unless your country's consumer law lets you bring a claim where you live. <span class="legal-placeholder">{CONFIRM}</span></li>
    <li><strong>Export:</strong> you'll comply with export control and sanctions laws that apply to you and the Software.</li>
    <li><strong>Severability:</strong> if part of this EULA is unenforceable, the rest stays in effect.</li>
    <li><strong>Entire agreement:</strong> this EULA, the <a href="/terms">terms of sale</a> and the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> are the whole agreement about the Software.</li>
    <li><strong>Changes:</strong> a later version of this EULA applies to an update only if you accept it when installing that update, and it will never reduce the number of Macs or end lifetime updates for a licence you own.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</LegalPage>
